  "id": "start-pitch-03-twos-and-threes",
  "title": "Twos and threes",
  "summary": "Spot the pattern of black keys that makes sense of the whole keyboard.",
  "order": 1,
  "skills": [
    "pitch.keyboard.layout"
  ],
  "prerequisites": [
    "start-pitch-02-up-down-or-the-same"
  ],
  "estimatedMinutes": 5,
  "newTerms": [],
  "steps": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "A piano has 88 keys, and nobody counts them. Pianists look at the black keys instead. Press the glowing ones, left to right. Can you see a pattern?",
      "exhibit": {
        "kind": "keyboard",
        "highlight": [
          "C#3",
          "D#3",
          "F#3",
          "G#3",
          "A#3",
          "C#4",
          "D#4",
          "F#4",
          "G#4",
          "A#4"
        ],
        "low": "C3",
        "high": "B4"
      }
    },
    "explore": {
      "text": "Play every black key, starting at the left. When you reach a gap in the black keys, stop and count how many you played in that group. Then carry on to the next group.",
      "instrument": "keyboard",
      "exhibit": {
        "kind": "keyboard",
        "highlight": [],
        "low": "C3",
        "high": "B4"
      },
      "goal": "Play every black key from the left and count the size of each group."
    },
    "name": {
      "cards": [
        {
          "text": "The black keys come in groups of **2** and groups of **3**. A group of 2, then a group of 3, then 2 again: 2, 3, 2, 3, all the way along the [[keyboard|keyboard]].",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "C#4",
              "D#4",
              "F#4",
              "G#4",
              "A#4"
            ],
            "low": "C4",
            "high": "B4"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The pattern works like a map. Each white key has its own spot, beside a group or between two black keys. The glowing white keys here all sit between the two black keys of a group of 2.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "D3",
              "D4"
            ],
            "low": "C3",
            "high": "B4"
          }
        }
      ],
      "alternative": {
        "text": "Picture a street where the houses come in blocks: a block of 2, then a block of 3, then 2, then 3. You know where you are by the block, not by counting every door. On the keyboard, find the block first. Then find your key beside it."
      }
    },
    "practice": {
      "questions": [
